<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Skoda signs deal with Mitsubishi.</title>
<headline>Czech Skoda signs deal with Mitsubishi.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech engineering concern Skoda a.s. and Japan's Mitsubishi Heavy Industries have signed a cooperation agreement in the field of steam turbines, a Skoda statement said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The statement added that Skoda had also concluded a deal with Russian firm Ljulka Saturn for 16 megawatt gas turbines, and obtained a licence to sell steam turbines produced by South Korea's Hyundai Heavy Industry.</p>
<p>The statement gave no further details on any of the agreements.</p>
<p>Plzen-based Skoda's production range spreads from beer cans to trucks and nuclear reactors. It is no longer affiliated with Volkswagen AG's Czech unit, car maker Skoda Automobilova a.s..</p>
